From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Quiet the stop, flag the timestamps

A stream stops from the VFE up: between the VFE's stop and the CSID's,
the frames the sensor still sends overflow the CSID path FIFOs and then
the receiver, which reported CRC and FIFO errors and marked the VFE
wedged on most stops. Ignore CSID errors while no VFE line it feeds
takes frames.

The pixel path, display and statistics buffers carry the frame start
time: flag their queues V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TSTAMP_SRC_SOE. RDI buffers keep
their completion time, which their default flags describe, also while
the pixel path numbers them. A wedged pixel path writes no more display
frames: do not wait for them when stopping.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
